---
kind: quest
id: term.quests
title: This term's errands
---

// Three paper lanterns for the dorm window by festival night (day 6 evening is
// clock.index 17). Hangouts fold them.
<quest id="festivalPrep" title="Fold three lanterns for the festival" start="true">
  <objective id="fold" title="Fold three lanterns before the festival" done="run.lanterns >= 3" by="clock.index >= 17"/>
  <on event="questComplete">
    @nana{code="0010" emotion="happy"}: Three! That's three! Our window won't be the dark one this year.
  </on>
  <on event="questFailed">
    @nana{code="0020" emotion="sad"}: The festival's tonight and we've got two sad lanterns and a paper crane. It's fine. It's — it's fine.
  </on>
</quest>

// Soren offers a study group in the library; taken, it wants two sessions
// before the exam (day 4 morning is clock.index 9).
<quest id="studyGroup" title="Study with Soren before the midterm">
  <objective id="sessions" title="Study twice in the library before the exam" done="run.study >= 2" by="clock.index >= 9"/>
  <on event="questComplete">
    @soren{code="0010" emotion="happy"}: You'll be fine. Better than fine. Don't tell anyone I said so; they'll all want sessions.
  </on>
  <on event="questFailed">
    @soren{code="0020" emotion="sad" when="!holds('locked', ['soren'])"}: We ran out of evenings. You'll still be fine. Probably.
  </on>
</quest>

// (0.27) Lighting the dorm window is a weekly chore. Every Monday (weekday 0)
// the duty comes round again: `rearm` returns it to unset and `start` takes it
// straight back up. It is done once someone lit the lamps on or after this
// week's Monday (run.day - clock.weekday), so the rearm needs no counter reset.
<quest id="lampDuty" title="Light the dorm window this week" start="true" rearm="clock.weekday == 0">
  <objective id="light" title="Light the dorm lanterns before Sunday night" done="run.lampDay >= run.day - clock.weekday" by="clock.weekday == 6 && run.slot == 'evening'"/>
  <on event="questComplete">
    @nana{code="0010" emotion="happy"}: Look at that. A lit window, and I didn't even have to nag.
  </on>
  <on event="questFailed">
    @nana{code="0020" emotion="sad"}: Sunday night, dark window. The seniors are going to talk.
  </on>
</quest>
